  "id": "COMPOUND:22599 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Arisantetralone D appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step mechanism involving DNA polymerase iota, which is targeted by the compound. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by Perseal F and Trigoneoside IB, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests that Arisantetralone D may act as a modulator of DNA polymerase iota, potentially disrupting cellular processes in CCRF-HSB-2 cells. The final_score of 0.4912 indicates a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by the direct targeting of DNA polymerase iota and its downstream effects on CCRF-HSB-2. The mechanism appears to be mechanistically plausible, though further validation would be required to confirm the specific role of Arisantetralone D in the activation of CCRF-HSB-2.",
